The Lantern Keep
Rain has stopped. The old keep looms above you, dark except for one window high in the tower.
Legend says whoever reaches that window can leave this world behind.
Type 'help' to see what you can do.

Outer Gate
You stand before the outer gate of the keep. The portcullis is rusted open just enough to squeeze through. The sky burns orange behind the battlements.
Exits: north.

> help
Commands
  help              show this list
  look              describe where you are
  go <direction>    move: north, south, east, west, up, down
  n/s/e/w/u/d       shortcuts for go
  take <item>       pick something up
  drop <item>       put something down
  inventory         list what you carry
  examine <item>    look closely at an item
  music             turn the background music on/off
  volume <0-100>    set the master volume
  clear             clear the screen
  quit              leave the game

> north

Courtyard
A quiet courtyard under a sky full of stars. An old stone well sits in the middle. A door leads east into the library; a dark hall lies to the north.
You see: lantern.
Exits: south, east, north.

> take lantern
You take the lantern.

> east

Library
Shelves of crumbling books reach up into the dark. A single candle flickers on the reading desk.
You see: key.
Exits: west.

> take key
You take the key.

> x key
A heavy brass key, warm to the touch.

> inventory
You are carrying: lantern, key.

> west

Courtyard
A quiet courtyard under a sky full of stars. An old stone well sits in the middle. A door leads east into the library; a dark hall lies to the north.
Exits: south, east, north.

> north

Great Hall
A long hall lit by two guttering torches. At the far end, a heavy oak door with a brass lock guards the tower stairs.
Exits: south, up.

> up
You unlock the door.

Tower Top
At the top of the stairs, the window opens onto a swirling, impossible sky. It pulls at you gently.
Exits: down.

You step through the window and fall upward into the light. THE END.
You finished in 5 moves. Type 'quit' to leave.

> music
The story is over. Type 'quit' to leave.

> quit
Farewell.
